constants: drop netfs from the device GKI module list

CONFIG_CIFS=y selects NETFS_SUPPORT=y, which builds netfs into vmlinux and stops
producing fs/netfs/netfs.ko. The device target's extracted_system_dlkm step reads
PIXEL_GKI_MODULES_LIST and fails when netfs.ko is absent from the built system_dlkm,
so drop its entry here to match. Companion to the common/gki/modules.bzl edit that
does the same for the GKI kernel build.

--- a/private/devices/google/common/constants.bzl
+++ b/private/devices/google/common/constants.bzl
@@ -50,7 +50,6 @@
     "drivers/virtio/virtio_pci.ko",
     "drivers/virtio/virtio_pci_legacy_dev.ko",
     "drivers/virtio/virtio_pci_modern_dev.ko",
-    "fs/netfs/netfs.ko",
     "kernel/kheaders.ko",
     "lib/crypto/libarc4.ko",
     "mm/zsmalloc.ko",
